  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/1b56e536-0167-431d-a969-0ebcdb0e36a2-image.png\" style=\"width: 492px; height: 150px;\" /></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>Ag</mi><mo>(</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><msubsup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo></msubsup><msup><mi>OH</mi><mo>-</mo></msup></math>&nbsp;is called&nbsp;Tollens&#39; reagent and it is a mild oxidizing reagent that oxidizes aldehyde groups to their respective acid and it gets reduced. It does not affect ketone group. While&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NaBH</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is a reducing agent which can reduce aldehyde or ketone group in alcohols but it&nbsp;does not reduce carboxylic acid.</p></blockquote>",
